cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use sqlguardllm in research or in a publication, please cite it as below."
title: "sqlguardllm: the SQL firewall for LLM apps"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, offline guard that validates SQL written by large language models and
  rewrites it so it is read-only, limited to allowlisted tables and columns, filtered per user
  with derived tables, and bounded in rows, across the SQL dialects supported by sqlglot.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Castillo
    given-names: Juan
repository-code: "https://github.com/jmmana/sqlguardllm"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - sql
  - large language models
  - text-to-sql
  - security
  - row-level security
  - sqlglot
